      <h3>History</h3>
      <p>An audit walks a bin and marks each expected item present or missing, and anything found that wasn't expected as extra. Moves, audits and description changes each append an event, and committing an audit never wipes earlier history. Around that:</p>
      <ul class='sub'>
        <li class='sub'><strong>Move all to&hellip;</strong> - empties a bin into another one in a single confirmed action, with a move event for every item</li>
        <li class='sub'><strong>Provenance</strong> - each item has a timeline of where it has been and what changed</li>
        <li class='sub'><strong>Collections</strong> - group items by purpose across bins, with a CSV export per collection</li>
        <li class='sub'><strong>Archiving</strong> - a bin can be archived once it is empty, and drops out of the pickers while keeping its history</li>
        <li class='sub'><strong>Conflicts</strong> - doing something that doesn't make sense, like moving an item into an archived bin, gets a clean 409 explaining why</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Claim gaps</h3>
      <p>A claim gaps view lists every item missing a serial, a replacement value or a receipt, with each row linking straight to that item's edit page. It turns "am I covered?" into a to-do list.</p>

      <h3>Platform</h3>
      <ul class='sub'>
        <li class='sub'>One Go binary, on SQLite or Postgres, with a Bootstrap UI</li>
        <li class='sub'>SSO at the gateway through an ext_authz OIDC flow, with passkeys from the identity provider</li>
        <li class='sub'>CSRF protection on every state change, rate limits, audit logging and CSP headers</li>
        <li class='sub'>Deployed by GitOps to the homelab cluster, with Go and JavaScript test suites gating CI</li>
      </ul>

